Arara Code: product default settings and keybindings (Windows/Linux).

- src/vs/workbench/common/arara.defaults.ts: registerDefaultConfigurations()
  with native settings only (editor, workbench, explorer, scm/git,
  typescript/javascript built-ins). Third-party extension settings are not
  included. Keybindings list in keybindings.json format ("-cmd" = removal).
- keybindingService: inject the Arara keybindings into the *default* layer of
  the resolver (not macOS), so the user can still override/remove them.
- workbench.common.main: import the defaults.
- test: entries parse; no third-party commands.

Why a patch: product.json cannot set configuration defaults or default
keybindings; an extension could, but would load late and show up as
"extension" defaults.
Touches: src/vs/workbench/common/arara.defaults.ts (new),
         src/vs/workbench/test/common/arara.defaults.test.ts (new),
         src/vs/workbench/services/keybinding/browser/keybindingService.ts,
         src/vs/workbench/workbench.common.main.ts

